# Following the Windows light/dark switch.
#
# The run poses the OS — nothing here reads the real machine, which is the point: these pictures
# have to be the same on every developer's PC, and the setting they are about is one that differs
# from desk to desk. `system-theme` is what Windows is set to and `system-follow` is whether the
# app cares, deliberately kept apart so a script can pose a switch that is being ignored.
#
# Read as a set. The interesting frames are the two transitions: high contrast arriving over a
# configured pair, and coming back off it to the right side rather than to Dark+.

tree .
refresh
select notes.txt

system-follow on
system-theme dark
assert-theme dark-plus
shot 01-follow-dark
dialog settings-appearance 02-appearance-following

system-theme light
assert-theme light-plus
shot 03-follow-light

# A configured pair rather than the two defaults, so a slot being ignored is visible.
system-slot light solarized-light
system-slot dark nord
assert-theme solarized-light
shot 04-light-slot-solarized
dialog settings-appearance 05-appearance-slots-set

system-theme dark
assert-theme nord
shot 06-dark-slot-nord

# High contrast overrides both slots, live...
system-theme high-contrast
assert-theme high-contrast-dark
shot 07-high-contrast
dialog settings-appearance 08-appearance-high-contrast

# ...and turning it off lands back on the dark slot, not on Dark+. This is what the two-switch
# SystemAppearance exists for: the light/dark bit is kept underneath high contrast rather than
# replaced by it.
system-theme dark
assert-theme nord
shot 09-back-on-nord

# Setting the slot for the mode Windows is *not* in configures without previewing: still Nord.
system-slot light catppuccin-latte
assert-theme nord

# Not following: the single picker, the way it has always looked. Unticking keeps what is on
# screen rather than jumping back to whatever was last selected.
system-follow off
assert-theme nord
assert-following off
dialog settings-appearance 10-appearance-not-following
shot 11-not-following

# The OS moving now changes nothing at all.
system-theme light
assert-theme nord

# And choosing a theme by hand is itself what stops following — the two pickers are the way to
# configure one without leaving the mode.
system-follow on
assert-theme catppuccin-latte
theme monokai
assert-following off
system-theme dark
assert-theme monokai
